#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn how to install snap on Red Hat Enterprise Linux with EPEL, enable the "
"socket and classic support, and refresh system paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:8
msgid "Install snap on Red Hat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:10
msgid ""
"Snap is available for [Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) 9.x](https://"
"developers.redhat.com/products/rhel/overview), RHEL 8 and RHEL 7, from the "
"7.6 release onwards. It's also available for CentOS 7.6+ (see {ref}"
"`Installing snap on CentOS <interfaces-installing-snap-on-centos>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:12
msgid ""
"The packages for RHEL are in the distribution's respective [Extra Packages "
"for Enterprise Linux](https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/EPEL) (EPEL) "
"repository. The instructions for adding this repository diverge slightly "
"between RHEL9, RHEL 8 and RHEL 7, which is why they're listed separately "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:14
msgid ""
"If you need to know which version of Red Hat you're running, type `cat /etc/"
"redhat-release`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:16
msgid ""
"If you don't already have the EPEL repository added to your distribution, it "
"can be added as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:18
msgid "Add EPEL to RHEL 9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:20
msgid ""
"The EPEL repository can be added to a RHEL 9 system with the following "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:22
msgid ""
"sudo dnf install https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/epel-release-"
"latest-9.noarch.rpm\n"
"sudo dnf upgrade\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:27
msgid "Add EPEL to RHEL 8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:29
msgid ""
"The EPEL repository can be added to a RHEL 8 system with the following "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:31
msgid ""
"sudo dnf install https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/epel-release-"
"latest-8.noarch.rpm\n"
"sudo dnf upgrade\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:36
msgid "Installing snapd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:38
msgid ""
"With the EPEL repository added to your RHEL installation, the next step is "
"to install the *snapd* package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:40
msgid "sudo yum install snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:44
msgid ""
"Once installed, the *systemd* unit that manages the main snap communication "
"socket needs to be enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:46
msgid "sudo systemctl enable --now snapd.socket\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:50
msgid ""
"To enable *classic* snap support, enter the following to create a symbolic "
"link between `/var/lib/snapd/snap` and `/snap`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:52
msgid "sudo ln -s /var/lib/snapd/snap /snap\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:56
msgid ""
"**Either log out and back in again or restart your system** to ensure snap’s "
"paths are updated correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/red-hat.md:58
msgid "Snap is now installed and ready to go."
msgstr ""
